## Code for the sampling design, reference data processing, and accuracy assessment of the disturbance maps.

Spatial accuracy
Temporal accuracy
Country-level accuracy

Original sampling design allocated an equal number of samples within disturbed and undisturbed areas, 
To account for sampling biases when deriving map accuracies, we follow the general recommendations by 
Olofsson et al. (2014), accounting for disproportionate probability sampling using known population 
proportions of the sampling strata (fweights). We incorporated the weights through weighted bootstrap 
resampling instead of weighting the confusion matrix. Weights were derived from the previous disturbance map 
(EFDA v2) used to construct the reference dataset: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22101910 
See Viana-Soto et al. (2026) for more details
